.hw 	vepos 	Puniv; Pnomgl  	indicative nominalizer; subordinatornote	ve is the most important particle in Black Lahu; see GL passim, esp. the sections listed in the Index Verborum, pp. 663-4; < PLB *way£ < PTB *way  & *ray; ve prob. reflects a PST/PTB copular morpheme [see JAM 1985b "God and the ST copula"]; for a discussion of ve in the context of general grammatical theory, see JAM 1972b "Lahu nominalization, relativization, and genitivization"ngl 	1. used in citation-forms of verbs, like Eng. tonote	NOTE: In this dictionary verbs and VP's are cited with ve when they appear as subentries; when a verb occurs as the head-entry the ve is omitted, and it is marked only by the form-class symbol "(V)"...hw 	qay ve                      pos 	Vgl  	to go..hw 	qhÈa ve                     pos 	Vgl  	to be bitterex  	vi ve lä fÑ” ve l\ä c|•-k\• \a-l\a=qhe qha-Çsw|” y\o -- \¿-khÈ¿ t|” pún d\aÖ ve xx  	                                   To dry out and to dry up mean more or xx  	                                   less the same -- only the sounds are xx  	                                   different.bz  	[clause-final] ngl 	2. indicative nominalizer: imparts a certain objectivity or neutrality to the verbal eventex  	yÈ¿ k\aÖ qay ve exgl	a. He goes too.ngl 	b. He's going too.ngl 	c. He'll go too.ngl 	d. He went too.ex  	yÈ¿ k\aÖ qay ve n\¿ ÇsÑ” \a lÈa exgl	Do you know that he's going/went/will go too?ex  	LÈahÑu-khÈ¿ hÈe ve l\ä Ùga te ve m¿ jÈa exgl	It takes a long time to learn Lahu ("As for learning Lahu, [one's] having to do it is a long time")...hw 	d\” ve Na-ph\oÖgl  	cha -- m\ä ve t\¿-q|u=ÇsÑä --..hw 	qhÈa ve y\ä-y|a-k•    --  ci ve pÈä-y|a-ci  --xx  	     qhÈa ve y\ä-y|a-k•    --  ci ve pÈä-y|a-ci  --ex  	n\u ve |a-v\a=vÈ”      exgl	Juicy is the pussy of Na-ph\oÖ -- ["that which is juicy is...; to be juicy is...; juiciness is..."] tasty is liver of turtle -- bitter is gall of bear -- sour are the larvae of the mÈún-c\eÖ bee -- stinking is the fart of a Wa! [children's jingle]bz  	[subordinator of NP to NP] ngl 	3. genitivizer..hw 	qhÈaÖ-Çsä ve \¿-khÈ¿pos 	NPgengl  	the headman's voice..hw 	phÈ•-Çse ve ÙgÈu-tu=ÇsÑ”pos 	NPgengl  	a flea's navel..hw 	³\a ve |a-p\oÖ ve p¿-hÈoÖ=t|äpos 	NPgengl  	the pocket of my shirt ("pocket of shirt of me")ngl 	4. relativizer (subordinator of clauses or clause-like adverbials to noun-heads)..hw 	yÈ¿ ÇsÑ” gÈa ve \¿-l¿pos 	LRC + Nrhgl  	the things that he wants to know..hw 	v\aÖ=|o-qÑo cÈ¿ Ña vepos 	Nrh + RRCgl  	a pig's head that has been boiled..hw 	n|” \ä ve |a-p\oÖpos 	AEstat + Nhgl  	a red shirt; a shirt that is red..hw 	|a-p\oÖ n|” \ä vepos 	Nh + AEstatgl  	a red shirt; a shirt that is red ngl 	5. correlative quantifier (in polyquantified NP's); Q1 per Q2..hw 	tÈe l\”Ö ve ³Èa chi b\aÖpos 	QQgl  	fifty baht per (one) liter..hw 	tÈe ha-pa ve nÈ” pÈ¿Öpos 	QQgl  	twice a month ("2 times per 1 month").hw 	ve-Ñ¿pos 	Pufgl  	emphatic final particle (used e.g. when giving insistent explanations)note	see GL 4.728; the 2nd element is prob. to be identified with Ñ¿ (Punf) 'topicalizer' [q.v.]ex  	a-c|” cä t|” ve-Ñ¿ exgl	There's only a little bit, you know!ex  	chi-b\úÖ mÈa-mÈa-mÈa-Ùg\• ve-Ñ¿ exgl	Now, you see, we are not numerous and few in number!ex  	LÈahÑu-yÈa t|” qo m\”-g\•=qhÈo mÈa ve k\aÖ mÈa hÈeÖ ve-Ñ¿ exgl	There aren't too many Lahu in the world either, you know!ex  	n\¿-h• ÙgÈa ve mÈa hÈeÖ ve-Ñ¿ exgl	Hey, you didn't win!.hw 	vÈe(n)pos 	Nloan	LOANgl  	*town; *citynote	< Shan wi³ [Cu 617] (cf. Siamese wia³ 'walled city', and names of cities like wia³can 'Vientiane'); cf. mÈú(n) (Bn)..hw 	vÈe­\¿=kh|•-pÑ•pos 	Ngl  	principal town of a region; *capital city..hw 	vÈe-qh¿ qay vepos 	Nloc + Vgl  	go to town; make a trip to the city..hw 	vÈe-khÑäpos 	Ngl  	name of a RL village in Thailand..hw 	vÈe=tÑa-m\úÖpos 	Ngl  	city wall..hw 	vÈe­tÑa-m\úÖ=ph\eÖpos 	Ngl  	gate in a city wall..